1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
That clunk when you shift into reverse

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,000
isn't nothing.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
A knock right as the driveshaft

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
takes up slack — worse backing out of the driveway.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,800
One clue: a worn universal joint,

6
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,000
where the driveshaft connects to the axle.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Left alone, that play can turn into a vibration —

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
or worse, down the road.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Don't guess. A quick check underneath

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
can find the play before it gets worse.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking before a small clunk becomes a bigger repair.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
